# Proposed by an executor (2026-10-15); the documenter may edit or drop it.
# Story: a laptop beside a monitor, nothing docked, mail on the monitor. The monitor's cable is pulled and mail waits on
# the laptop. Arbor is quit; its person drags mail to where they want it on the lap, and starts Arbor again. Next morning the
# monitor is plugged in: mail stays where it was put. Arbor used to take it back to the monitor: a drag it sees has always
# ended the monitor's claim, one it did not see had not.
# And what must stay. Notes waited beside it and nobody touched it: it goes home. Then: quit at the desk, the cable pulled while
# Arbor is not running, a start on the lap. macOS had to move Notes, which is nobody's hand: back at the desk it goes home.
# Reference: rule 2 (nothing moves until the person docks something); collab/QUESTIONS.md, "a hand Arbor did not see".
plug side right 1920x1080
open Mail 700x500
open Notes 600x400
move 101 1600 100 700 500
move 102 2400 500 600 400
wait 3
quietly unplug side
move 101 160 100 700 500
move 102 840 475 600 400
wait 1.7
report-displays
wait 3
expect visible 101
expect visible 102
relaunch quit
move 101 500 300 700 500
relaunch start
expect still
wait 3
quietly plug side right 1920x1080
wait 1.7
report-displays
wait 3
expect at 101 500 300
expect size 101 700x500
expect floating 101
expect at 102 2400 500
# Quit at the desk, the cable pulled meanwhile, a start on the lap, back at the desk.
relaunch quit
quietly unplug side
move 102 840 475 600 400
relaunch start
wait 3
expect visible 102
quietly plug side right 1920x1080
wait 1.7
report-displays
wait 3
expect at 102 2400 500
expect at 101 500 300
